  "id": "anchoring-bias",
  "term": "anchoring bias",
  "definition": "Anchoring bias is a thinking bias in which an earlier piece of information acts as a reference point and pulls later judgments in the same direction. In the source example, a supplier’s past score in one area influenced how people rated that supplier in other areas and how likely they were to choose the supplier again.",
